      "writtenOn": "2022-01-27T23:25:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought about this, but when I tested the code like so:\n- boot device with unmodified logd (so nothing reads /dev/trusty-log0)\n- read+poll /dev/trusty-log0 once (so it reads until the end)\n- run \"tipc-test -t echo\", which causes one line of trusty logging\n- cause a panic (this should now dump that one line of logging to the kernel log)\nWhat I saw with some added logging in the dump_logs function was that \"get\" and \"last_successful_next\" had different values, and using the \"get\" value would not have dumped that last log line to the kernel log.\nI did not investigate further but I\u0027ll check again to make sure I didn\u0027t miss anything.",
      "parentUuid": "a2823f78_4e281c5d",
